    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=16$.",
      "worked": "Here, $n$ is the number of positive integers being added. Substitute $S=136$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{n}{2}(n+1)&=136\\\\n(n+1)&=272\\\\n^2+n-272&=0\\\\(n+17)(n-16)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy the null factor law, $n=-17$ or $n=16$. Since $n$ must be a positive integer, $n=16$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
